{
  "comment": "The caller public verify keys the shared application render takes as a render-time input and writes, comma-joined, into the proxy container's CURIE_CALLER_PROXY_PUBLIC_KEYS (ADR 0239 identity contract 2, ADR 0194 parity). A key is the canonical standard base64, padded, of a 32-byte Ed25519 public key: one spelling per key, so stray trailing bits refuse. At most max_keys: the current key, then the one it replaced during a rotation. Checks run in precedence order and the first that fails names the refusal. The two well-formed keys are the public keys frozen in connector-caller-token.json.",
  "env": "CURIE_CALLER_PROXY_PUBLIC_KEYS",
  "max_keys": 2,
  "precedence": [
    "caller_public_keys_empty",
    "caller_public_keys_too_many",
    "caller_public_key_malformed",
    "caller_public_keys_duplicate"
  ],
